        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T16:58:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the idea is that MMap profiles served by the DSP have their profiles filled out statically, like here, both for output and input mix ports: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:device/google/redfin/audio/audio_policy_configuration.xml;l\u003d72;drc\u003d53acf6b56a56ef4e84b3b10ac425c9a7ade15aa7\n\nAFAIK, none of AOSP non-primary modules (the USB module being the primary concern) support MMap. Thus, in my understanding this should work fine unless for some reason MMap mix ports have dynamic profiles. Are there any examples of devices that use them in such configuration?",
      "parentUuid": "f62f73f4_4f6dfe22",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f0c5c118851e84617489be44e864d63e3dc79283",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84ebf8f3_710226b6",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T17:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be too constraining to mandate that MMAP IOs are never using dynamic profiles. \nDoes this problem still exist with AIDL HALs were we do not need to open the stream to probe for port properties?",
      "parentUuid": "cec00652_249c543d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f0c5c118851e84617489be44e864d63e3dc79283",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d712e5d_5db22b15",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T17:20:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As of now, the problem still exists because the framework still uses the legacy path even using the AIDL HAL. In fact, for QC some metrics got regressed because in the AIDL opening an MMap No IRQ stream requires creating the shared memory region (this was a separate operation in the HIDL API).\n\nAs a long term solution we need to avoid using this legacy probing path when using the AIDL HAL. Maybe, as a short term solution we can update this patch to only avoid opening MMap I/Os for probing when they don\u0027t have dynamic profiles?",
      "parentUuid": "84ebf8f3_710226b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f0c5c118851e84617489be44e864d63e3dc79283",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4d12ab7_52e48544",
        "filename": "services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 6635,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T21:02:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is going to be skipped for mmap profiles, as I understand it. I guess, that means that corresponding mix ports will not have their profiles populated. I think, this may be important for \"hifi\" mix ports that in some implementations skip SRC paths in DSP and thus must show actual sampling rates and other parameters of the connected device.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6635,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6635,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "f0c5c118851e84617489be44e864d63e3dc79283",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e71ce4fa_92a9e7a2",
        "filename": "services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 6635,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527754
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T03:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per my understanding \"hifi\" and \"mmap\" are going to be different mix ports. \n\nMMAP is supposed to be meant to be used for clients using MAP_NOIRQ flags and speicifying supported samplerates/other params.\n\nFor hifi_playback paths, I have not seen any specific flags defined, and profiles are kept empty, so it can be retrieved based on device ports. So, fundamentally \"hifi\" and \"mmap\" are different and I think we are not going to touch \"hifi\" path with this change.\n\nAlso, as this whole logic of opening outputs and closing the outputs, is needed only to see if the any existing playback can be routed to 1 of newly opened output.\n\nFor MMAP, we should not be doing that, unless the client explicitly asks for mmap flags. \n\nAfter, connection, if client tries to open a mmap, they can do that anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "c4d12ab7_52e48544",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6635,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6635,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "f0c5c118851e84617489be44e864d63e3dc79283",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
